# LLM layer

This is the ONLY place the OpenAI SDK may be imported — specifically
`app/llm/openai_provider.py`. Nothing outside `app/llm/` imports `openai`.
If a task seems to need the SDK elsewhere, the answer is a method on
`LLMProvider`, not an import.

## Implementations

- `openai_provider.py` — thin adapter. Maps SDK exceptions to typed domain
  errors (`ProviderTimeout`, `ProviderUnavailable`, `RateLimited`,
  `InvalidRequest`) and SDK usage to our `Usage` object. No policy lives here.
- `resilient.py` — the decorator holding ALL policy: timeout budget, selective
  bounded retry, circuit breaker, degradation. Everything above it is oblivious.
  `timeout_s` on `LLMProvider.complete` is owned here: only the decorator
  computes remaining budget and passes a deadline down. `ask.py` (and anything
  else above the decorator) must never pass `timeout_s` — if it does, budget
  policy has leaked into the pipeline and the seam is cosmetic.
- `fake.py` — scriptable double for tests. Queue holds responses or exceptions.
- `chaos.py` — deliberate failure injection driven by env vars
  (`CHAOS_TIMEOUT_RATE`, `CHAOS_500_RATE`, `CHAOS_LATENCY_MS`). Used for the
  outage demo and manual soak testing.

## Retry policy — precise

- Retry ONLY on: 429, 5xx, timeouts, connection errors.
- NEVER retry: any 4xx, content-policy refusals, schema validation failures.
  A malformed request will be malformed the second time, at full price.
- Max 2 retries. Exponential backoff WITH jitter (without jitter, everything
  that failed together retries together).
- Before starting a retry, check both remaining time budget and remaining cost
  budget. If either would be breached, degrade instead of retrying.

## Circuit breaker

Closed → open after N consecutive failures → half-open probe after a short
window. Thresholds are configuration, never hardcoded constants in logic —
they are guesses that production data would replace.

## Prompts

Prompts live in `app/llm/prompts/*.md`, loaded and hashed at startup. The hash
is stored as `prompt_version` on every message row. Never inline a prompt as a
string literal. Keep prompts short: every token is paid for on every question.

Request structured output with a JSON schema AND validate the parsed object
yourself, failing closed on a mismatch. Provider-side schema enforcement is
very good and is not a guarantee.

Temperature 0 on the answering call.
